Package: lakefold
Title: Composable R Workflows for Governed Data Products
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: person("Jan-Hendrik", "Weinert", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "65009403+JanWein@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Combines reusable specifications and explicit execution steps for
    ingesting data, validating immutable candidates, publishing versioned data
    products and calculating governed metrics. Supports concise entry points and
    composition of more complex workflows using ordinary R functions and lazy
    tidyverse queries. Uses DuckLake or a local DuckDB backend, optional pointblank
    validation, dm models and a read-only Shiny catalog. Runs dbt through its
    command-line interface and exposes results, dependency lineage and relational
    models in R.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports: DBI, duckdb (>= 1.5.5), dplyr (>= 1.1.0), dbplyr, tibble, rlang, digest, jsonlite
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), pointblank, dm, shiny, bslib, yaml,
    readr, readxl, paws.storage, knitr, rmarkdown, processx, withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/Needs/website: pkgdown, DiagrammeR, DiagrammeRsvg
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
